meta {
  name: stats-range
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/admin/v1/stats/range?from=2026-08-01&to=2026-08-31
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{access_token}}
}

tests {
  test("responds 200", function () {
    expect(res.status).to.equal(200)
  })
}

docs {
  # A date range

`YYYY-MM-DD`, parsed in the restaurant's timezone, `to` inclusive.

Capped at 366 days: an unbounded range is a cheap way to make the database scan the whole orders
table. An inverted range or a malformed date answers 400 rather than being silently ignored --
dropping a date filter would return the entire history where one day was asked for, which looks like
data corruption rather than a bad parameter.
}
